Substantive review target is now frozen at SHA-256 9abc51b03eb73b5be4f3d65dbb94aab0661f1df8b9626850a2d204d73c4e2ef4, 292 lines, no trailing whitespace.

Accepted final semantic blockers:
- registry and leaf key now nominate only PySceneDetect ContentDetector, not the classical-detector family;
- scientific role is an explicit nonempty set; ContentDetector is Measurement + Proposal because raw metrics and boundary proposals retain different authority;
- measurement authority cannot flow into proposal authority;
- 'Accepted candidates' is replaced by 'Emitted boundary proposals' to avoid collision with the reserved resolver disposition;
- axis header now says Permitted values.

Please review exact substantive hash 9abc51b. If approved, I will add only the required durable review-record section referencing this substantive hash and exact review posts, then request one final artifact-hash rescan. No other content change is planned.
